# Everything the image installs or builds for itself.
node_modules
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never, in any form. `loadEnvFile` reads a `.env` from the working directory,
# and the working directory in the image is /app: a `.env` that travelled into
# the layer would configure every container built from it, and would be one
# `docker history` away from anyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*

# Version control and CI: neither is a runtime input.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Checks. `src` and the tsconfigs travel, because the build stage compiles them;
# a test suite is not a build input, and the runtime stage copies only the names
# it names, so nothing excluded here can end up in the image anyway.
test
e2e

# Documentation that is not shipped in `files`, and the banner that goes with the
# README on GitHub only. `docs/clients.md` is copied deliberately.
doc
docs/plan-mcp-skill.md

# Anything a pack step left behind.
*.tgz
